 "cells":[
  {"cell_type":"markdown","id":"phase1-title","metadata":{},"source":["# AnimalEmotion AI – Deep Learning-Based Animal Emotion Recognition System\n","## Phase 1: Dataset Audit\n","\n","Evidence-driven inspection of the Kaggle dataset; no model training, train/validation/test split, or source-image modification. Dataset: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/kk2004/animalemotion/data\n","\n","Labels are only considered verified when an analyst explicitly confirms annotation columns in the review configuration. Folder names and suggestive column names alone are not authoritative."]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","id":"audit-plan","metadata":{},"source":["## Audit plan\n","Safe download/extraction; recursive inventory; integrity and format classification; EXIF-aware visual review; dimensions, channels, file sizes; exact and optional scalable near-duplicate detection; annotation-to-image mapping; label and subject overlap review; leakage risks; machine-readable reports and downloadable bundle. Empty datasets are represented with explicit schemas.\n","\n","This notebook avoids destructive cleanup. Unsupported HEIC/HEIF decoding is reported separately from unreadable supported formats. Human review remains necessary for mapping and label semantics."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","id":"setup-imports","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["from pathlib import Path\n","import os, sys, json, zipfile, hashlib, stat, shutil, random, re, subprocess, datetime, time, platform, ast\n","import numpy as np, pandas as pd\n","from PIL import Image, ImageOps, UnidentifiedImageError, ImageFile\n","from tqdm.auto import tqdm\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt, seaborn as sns\n","import torch, torchvision, cv2, sklearn\n","try:\n","    import psutil\n","except Exception:\n","    psutil=None\n","SEED=42; random.seed(SEED); np.random.seed(SEED); torch.manual_seed(SEED)\n","if torch.cuda.is_available(): torch.cuda.manual_seed_all(SEED)\n","torch.backends.cudnn.deterministic=True; torch.backends.cudnn.benchmark=False; sns.set_theme(style='whitegrid')\n","ROOT=Path('/content/animalemotion'); RAW=ROOT/'raw'; DATA=ROOT/'dataset'; REPORTS=ROOT/'reports'\n","for folder in (ROOT,RAW,DATA,REPORTS): folder.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)\n","print('Python',platform.python_version(),'| torch',torch.__version__,'| torchvision',torchvision.__version__,'| GPU',torch.cuda.is_available())\n","if torch.cuda.is_available(): print(torch.cuda.get_device_name(0))\n","def resource_snapshot(stage):\n","    row={'stage':stage,'utc':datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat(),'rss_bytes':None,'available_memory_bytes':None}\n","    if psutil:\n","        try:\n","            proc=psutil.Process(); row.update(rss_bytes=proc.memory_info().rss,available_memory_bytes=psutil.virtual_memory().available)\n","        except Exception as exc: row['error']=str(exc)\n","    return row\n","resource_log=[resource_snapshot('setup')]"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","id":"kaggle-auth-heading","metadata":{},"source":["## Kaggle authentication and download\n","Configure `KAGGLE_USERNAME` and `KAGGLE_KEY` through Colab Secrets, or use the secure `kaggle.json` upload fallback. Credentials are not hardcoded or included in reports. Download timestamp, archive hashes, dataset version/metadata, license fields, and a usage-review checklist are recorded."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","id":"kaggle-download","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["subprocess.run([sys.executable,'-m','pip','install','-q','kaggle'],check=True)\n","username=key=None\n","try:\n","    from google.colab import userdata\n","    username,key=userdata.get('KAGGLE_USERNAME'),userdata.get('KAGGLE_KEY')\n","except Exception: pass\n","kaggle_cfg=Path.home()/'.kaggle'/'kaggle.json'; kaggle_cfg.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)\n","if not (username and key) and kaggle_cfg.exists():\n","    try:\n","        cfg=json.loads(kaggle_cfg.read_text()); username,key=cfg.get('username'),cfg.get('key')\n","    except Exception as exc: print('Could not read token file:',exc)\n","if not (username and key):\n","    try:\n","        from google.colab import files\n","        print('Upload kaggle.json; token contents will not be displayed.')\n","        uploaded=files.upload()\n","        if 'kaggle.json' in uploaded:\n","            kaggle_cfg.write_bytes(uploaded['kaggle.json']); cfg=json.loads(kaggle_cfg.read_text()); username,key=cfg.get('username'),cfg.get('key')\n","    except Exception as exc: print('Token upload unavailable:',exc)\n","if not (username and key): raise RuntimeError('Kaggle credentials unavailable. Configure Colab Secrets or upload kaggle.json.')\n","kaggle_cfg.write_text(json.dumps({'username':username,'key':key})); os.chmod(kaggle_cfg,0o600)\n","os.environ['KAGGLE_USERNAME']=username; os.environ['KAGGLE_KEY']=key\n","SLUG='kk2004/animalemotion'; download_utc=datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat()\n","if not list(RAW.glob('*.zip')):\n","    proc=subprocess.run(['kaggle','datasets','download','-d',SLUG,'-p',str(RAW)],capture_output=True,text=True)\n","    if proc.returncode: raise RuntimeError('Kaggle download failed: '+proc.stderr[-2000:])\n","archives=sorted(RAW.glob('*.zip'))\n","if not archives: raise FileNotFoundError(f'No dataset ZIP found under {RAW}')\n","def file_sha256(path):\n","    h=hashlib.sha256()\n","    with open(path,'rb') as stream:\n","        for block in iter(lambda:stream.read(1024*1024),b''): h.update(block)\n","    return h.hexdigest()\n","archive_metadata=[{'name':p.name,'bytes':p.stat().st_size,'sha256':file_sha256(p)} for p in archives]\n","metadata_proc=subprocess.run(['kaggle','datasets','metadata',SLUG,'-p',str(RAW)],capture_output=True,text=True)\n","metadata_path=RAW/'dataset-metadata.json'; kaggle_metadata={}\n","if metadata_path.exists():\n","    try: kaggle_metadata=json.loads(metadata_path.read_text())\n","    except Exception as exc: print('Kaggle metadata parse error:',exc)\n","else: print('Kaggle metadata endpoint unavailable or metadata not downloaded:',metadata_proc.stderr[-500:])\n","license_files=[p for p in RAW.rglob('*') if p.is_file() and p.name.lower() in {'license','license.txt','licence','licence.txt'}]\n","print('Dataset archives:',[x['name'] for x in archive_metadata])"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","id":"safe-extract-heading","metadata":{},"source":["## Safe ZIP extraction\n","Reject absolute paths, parent traversal, symlinks, and resolved paths escaping the extraction root. Existing raw images are never edited or deleted."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","id":"safe-extract","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["def safe_extract(archive,destination):\n","    root=destination.resolve(); accepted=[]; rejected=[]\n","    with zipfile.ZipFile(archive) as zf:\n","        for info in zf.infolist():\n","            name=info.filename; rel=Path(name); mode=info.external_attr>>16\n","            if name.startswith('/') or re.match(r'^[A-Za-z]:',name) or '..' in rel.parts or stat.S_ISLNK(mode):\n","                rejected.append({'entry':name,'reason':'unsafe path or symbolic link'}); continue\n","            target=(root/rel).resolve()\n","            if target!=root and root not in target.parents:\n","                rejected.append({'entry':name,'reason':'resolved outside destination'}); continue\n","            if info.is_dir(): target.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True); continue\n","            target.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)\n","            with zf.open(info) as src,open(target,'wb') as dst: shutil.copyfileobj(src,dst)\n","            accepted.append(name)\n","    return accepted,rejected\n","accepted=[]; rejected=[]\n","for archive in archives:\n","    a,r=safe_extract(archive,DATA); accepted.extend(a); rejected.extend(r)\n","(REPORTS/'safe_extraction.json').write_text(json.dumps({'extracted_count':len(accepted),'rejected_entries':rejected},indent=2))\